# Trivy suppressions — risk-accepted dependency CVEs.
#
# These are the SAME acceptances pip-audit.yml already encodes via
# --ignore-vuln and SECURITY.md documents in full ("Accepted Dependency
# Risks"). Trivy was the only dependency scanner in the fleet without them, so
# every fs and image scan re-raised an alert the threat model had already
# dispositioned -- the reliable way to train an operator to ignore the
# Security tab entirely, which costs more than the finding it surfaces.
#
# Adding an entry here is a security decision, not housekeeping: it needs the
# matching SECURITY.md rationale and a review date, exactly as below.

# chromadb 1.5.9 — pre-auth RCE in Chroma SERVER mode (`chroma run` /
# HttpClient). CyClaw uses the embedded PersistentClient exclusively, in
# process, with no network listener, so the vulnerable path is unreachable in
# this deployment. Any change introducing chromadb.HttpClient or a standalone
# Chroma server re-opens this assessment.
#
# CVE-2026-45830/45831/45833 are siblings on the same HTTP-server surface
# (authenticated IDOR, RBAC scope bug, and post-auth code injection,
# respectively — see SECURITY.md for the per-CVE breakdown); pip-audit.yml
# added the same acceptance for all four on 2026-08-26. Added here 2026-08-27
# so Trivy's fs/image scans stop re-raising an already-accepted risk.
# Review: next chromadb release or 2026-10-01, whichever comes first.
CVE-2026-45829
CVE-2026-45830
CVE-2026-45831
CVE-2026-45833

# nltk 3.10.0 — no fixed release available. The advisory is a URL-encoded
# path-traversal reached through nltk.data.load(), i.e. the punkt tokenizer.
# CyClaw never calls nltk.data.load() and never loads punkt: retrieval/stemmer.py
# tokenizes with its own compiled regex (_WORD_RE) and imports only
# nltk.stem.PorterStemmer, a pure-Python stemmer that loads no data files. The
# vulnerable code path is therefore unreachable regardless of WHEN tokenization
# runs -- which matters, because tokenize_and_stem() runs both at corpus index
# time AND on every keyword query at request time.
# Guardrail: any change introducing nltk.data.load(), nltk.download(), or
# punkt/word_tokenize re-opens this assessment.
# Review: next nltk release or 2026-10-01, whichever comes first.
CVE-2026-12243
PYSEC-2026-597
